<li>
  <details class="details-reset details-overlay details-overlay-dark">
    <summary class="stat-toggle">
      <%= render Primer::Beta::Text.new(tag: :strong, color: view.allocations_scheme) do %>
        <%= view.obj_allocated %>
      <% end %> allocations
    </summary>

    <details-dialog class="anim-fade-in fast Box Box--overlay Box-overlay--wide d-flex flex-column" aria-label="Allocations explanation"><%# erblint:disable A11yDetailsDialogMigration %>
      <div class="Box-header">
        <button class="Box-btn-octicon btn-octicon float-right" type="button" aria-label="Close dialog" data-close-dialog>
          <%= render Primer::Beta::Octicon.new(icon: "x") %>
        </button>
        <h3>Allocations</h3>
      </div>

      <div class="Box-body overflow-auto">
        <p>This request made
          <%= render Primer::Beta::Text.new(tag: :strong, color: view.allocations_scheme) do %>
            <%= view.obj_allocated %>
          <% end %> allocations

          <% if view.allocations_scheme == :danger %>
            😭
          <% elsif view.allocations_scheme == :attention %>
            👀
          <% else %>
            🙂
          <% end %>
        </p>

        <p> &lt 300k allocations per request is acceptable. </p>
        <p> &lt 100k allocations per request is a good target. </p>

        <p>Too many allocations will result in worse performance
        as we spend more time in garbage collection.</p>

        See
        <%= render(Primer::Beta::Link.new(href: "https://thehub.github.com/epd/engineering/dev-practicals/performance/tools/allocation-tracer/", classes: "Link--inTextBlock", scheme: :default, underline: true)) { "Allocation Tracer docs" } %>
        for how to identify costly allocations.
      </div>
    </details-dialog>
  </details>
</li>
